    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Sharp intent Gu can condense sharp intent. That intent is very sharp, like swords and spears, but soft tactics can subdue it, and restoring it is very difficult. Fang Yuan weighs sharp intent against hostile intent and reckless intent while studying how to handle Mo Yao’s will, and concludes her will matches none of those three forms.",
        "chapters": [
          580
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "sharp-intent-effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_mo_yao"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Earlier, to deal with Mo Yao, Fang Yuan buys many wisdom path Gu worms, including special will Gu, deliberate will Gu, sharp intent Gu, and others. The wills those Gu form help him at the end of his northern plains journey, and later stand in for his own thinking under the light of wisdom when his brain cannot keep up.",
        "chapters": [
          652
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
